{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the people began to commit harlotry.</b> Their initial intent was not to serve idolatry at all, but only to commit harlotry. Yet what happened to them was exactly as the Torah warned when it prohibited intermarriage with the nations, as it says (Exodus 34:15–16): ״וְקָרָא לְךָ וְאָכַלְתָּ מִזִּבְחוֹ וְלָקַחְתָּ מִבְּנֹתָיו וְזָנוּ בְנֹתָיו וְהִזְנוּ אֶת בָּנֶיךָ אַחֲרֵי אֱלֹהֵיהֶן״." "<b>And the people ate and bowed down to their elohim.</b> For such is the way of the evil impulse: to proceed from one evil to another, as our Sages of blessed memory testified (Shabbat 105a)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:06.482203744Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}